        "outcome": {
            "name": "Hydrogen gas inhalation during PCI in STEMI patients was feasible and safe, with no HI-related severe adverse events. While the primary outcome (cardiac salvage index at 7 days) showed no significant difference between groups, the HI group showed significant improvement in surrogate outcomes at 6 months, including LV stroke volume index and a trend toward improved LV ejection fraction, suggesting potential benefit in promoting LV reverse remodeling.",
